Nuked OPL2 Lite: the crushed sample without shifting a negative number

OPL2_OutputCrush() drops the low bits of the sample, as the chip's output
stage does, by shifting it right and back left again. The sample is signed, and
the left shift of a negative number is undefined behaviour, which
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer stops the program at:

  src/chips/nuked/nukedopl2.c:863:12: runtime error: left shift of negative
  value -126

A multiplication says the same thing and is defined. The lines above clamp the
sample to -32768 to 32767 and the shift is at most 6, so the product is well
inside an int32_t.

This is ADLplug-Next's own patch, applied to the submodule by
cmake/Patches.cmake when CMake configures, and it goes away once the change is
upstream.

diff --git a/src/chips/nuked/nukedopl2.c b/src/chips/nuked/nukedopl2.c
index 940c7c6..4d8892d 100644
--- a/src/chips/nuked/nukedopl2.c
+++ b/src/chips/nuked/nukedopl2.c
@@ -860,7 +860,7 @@ static int16_t OPL2_OutputCrush(int32_t sample)
         shift = 0;
 
     sample >>= shift;
-    sample <<= shift;
+    sample *= 1 << shift;
 
     return (int16_t)sample;
 }
